ew resets, listing hook); inspected trailer commits 302d6064 and d0102317; ran artifact-check --strict, surface-check --strict, focused -race doctor tests, pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp and pose validate --strict; rechecked the spec requirement trace, known gaps and follow-ups against the code and evidence.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assumption-integrity\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-federated-spec-capture-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the material assumptions: memo soundness depends on closeoutChain being read only in localScopeClosed (verified by grep, closeout_review_policy.go:393); remote proofs are cut conservatively (verified by TestDoctorCloseoutMemoForeignSpecProofIsNotRetained); F5 timings are reported measurements in .pose/reports, not reproduced. Accepted risks R1-F1/R1-F2 are disclosed as open follow-ups, and the spec's R1 trace now says so. The implementer's surface-check claim is now verified true.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-concurrency\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-federated-spec-capture-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Memo and trace are mutex-guarded, no lock is held across recursive verification, and the memo is closed in a defer; focused tests pass under -race at d0102317.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-contracts\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-outcomes-v2-contract\", \"rationale\": \"No exported API, JSON or CLI/MCP shape changed; the new fields and listing hook are unexported.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-input-errors\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Errors, false results and cuts are never cached; a query error, then an audit error, takes precedence and no list is published.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Snapshots are allocated after the read view and before binding in both operation entries; remote crossings stay unmemoized; the doctor consumer at internal/cli/doctor.go:1616 is unchanged.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-observability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Audit and binding failures surface as doctor closeout-review.owed warnings with the error text and a remediation.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"compatibility\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the public CloseoutReviewsOwed and doctor output: legacy-unversioned instances keep the prior advisory path, versioned instances fail closed per R1, and the delivery-target declaration uses the existing format. No migration is needed.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"correctness\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-federated-spec-capture-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Reuse happens only when the ancestor chain is disjoint from the visited scopes, which suffices because cycle checks read only closeoutChain; equivalence with the plain verifier is tested for linear, ancestor-intersecting and cyclic topologies.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"design-causality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-30a434e2df6ef2a0\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the design against the profiled cause (repeated resolver catalogue parsing and repeated predecessor verification). D1's per-operation resolver snapshots address the parse cost (R2, counted by the specCatalogueListed hook); the bounded memo under D1/D2 addresses repeated terminal verification (R6). Both stay inside the audited operation, so the final audit (R1/R4) remains the correctness boundary.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"documentation\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-30a434e2df6ef2a0\", \"rationale\": \"Doctor output and the scaffold are unchanged, so no operational doc update is needed; the spec's delivery target, requirement trace (now qualified for R1), final report and follow-ups match the runtime behavior and the evidence.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"operability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Doctor still names `pose closeout-check <scope>` when the list cannot be produced; memo limits fall back to the original verifier rather than erroring.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"requirements\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-federated-spec-capture-integration\", \"rationale\": \"R1-R6 are traced to current tests and the registered check; surface-check --strict confirms the evidence is bound to the current provenance; the residual R1 public-path gap is a disclosed low follow-up.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scope\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-30a434e2df6ef2a0\", \"rationale\": \"Compared the change set with the spec's Artifacts and non-goals: only the declared implementation files changed; later rounds added only governance records and spec text; there is no persistent cache, new catalogue or policy change.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"security\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined authority boundaries: a dynamic Authorize disables the memo; missing, duplicate and unauthorized identities resolve identically to the live path; snapshots never cross operations; same-size edits with a restored mtime are refused by the final audit.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"solution-proportionality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-30a434e2df6ef2a0\", \"rationale\": \"Compared with the smallest alternative: snapshots alone were measured insufficient (>600 s), which justifies the memo. It is bounded (2048 entries, 256/32768 visited), confined to one callback, keeps only approvals, and has no persistence or extension points. The choice is invalidated if closeoutChain gains other readers, or if terminal verification comes to depend on caller state outside the guarded fields.\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"artifact-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-doctor-asks-every-closeout-in-one-operation --strict\", \"rationale\": \"Exit 0 on cs-618808f181bc (7 commits, 10 claims, 29 observed); the 978 warnings are orphan paths elsewhere in the repo.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-design\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; relied on the sealed structure evidence and direct code reading.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; the component surface was reviewed directly through the diff.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; integration impact was judged from sealed integration evidence and code reading.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; not needed to judge this bugfix scope.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is completion of this review; it cannot pass before the attestation.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is completion of this review; it cannot pass before the attestation.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; review targets were taken from the sealed change set.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"surface-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-federated-spec-capture-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Ran `pose surface-check --spec pose-doctor-asks-every-closeout-in-one-operation --strict` at d0102317: 1 target, 233 results, 0 findings.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"The sealed evidence passes. My sandboxed `pose validate --strict` exited 1 on the same 11 environment-bound checks as rounds 1 and 2 (/var/tmp ownership, an HTTP 403 on the release listing, runtime host start, chmod); none of them exercises the changed files.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-federated-spec-capture-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The sealed evidence passes. In my `pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp` run this scope's check passed; the run exited 1 only on the same 11 environment-bound checks.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":5011,"type":"result","duration_ms":2038740,"uuid":"00ee1b05-212e-41f0-a242-d0cc2e7b4b2c","ttft_stream_ms":4764,"time_to_request_ms":200,"first_content_frame_ms":4764,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":18,"outputTokens":8033,"cacheReadInputTokens":1261185,"cacheCreationInputTokens":26243,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.622913,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":318,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":26243,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-14T17:29:56.498Z"}
